-- title:
--   Weighted blow-up chart C[J/varpiₜ] and its exceptional valuation
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q$ and a nonzero natural number $M'$ with $q \nmid M'$, together with a prime $\ell$ satisfying $\ell \equiv 11 \pmod{12}$ and $\ell \mid M'$. Let $L$ be a field of characteristic $0$ and $\zeta \in L$ a primitive $q$-th root of unity; the hypothesis `hι` asserts that some ring homomorphism $\iota : L \to \mathbb{C}$ sends $\zeta$ to $e^{2\pi i/q}$. The subgroup $H_1 \le (\mathbb{Z}/q^2M')^\times$ is required (`hH₁`) to be the intersection of [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.levelH q M'`](def/ModularCurve_FullLevelJacobian.html#L22), the kernel of reduction $(\mathbb{Z}/q^2M')^\times \to (\mathbb{Z}/q)^\times$, with the kernel of reduction $(\mathbb{Z}/q^2M')^\times \to (\mathbb{Z}/\ell)^\times$; so $H_1$ consists of the units congruent to $1$ modulo $q$ and modulo $\ell$. The field $K$ is an intermediate field of $L \subseteq \mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,L$, required (`hK`) to equal [`ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange L (ModularCurve.xHFunctionField (q ^ 2 * M') H₁)`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L103), i.e. the $L$-subfield generated by the coefficientwise images under [`ModularCurve.coeffEmb L`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L81) of the $q$-expansion function field of the congruence subgroup `GammaH (q ^ 2 * M') H₁`.
--
--   The base ring $A$ is a discrete valuation ring which is a domain, an $L$-algebra with $L$ as its fraction field, Henselian local and with algebraically closed residue field; it is assumed that $q \in \mathfrak{m}_A$ (`hAq`) and that $\zeta$ lies in the image of $A$ (`hζA`), and $K$ is an $A$-algebra compatibly with $L$. The element $j \in K$ is required (`hj`) to have Laurent series [`ModularCurve.coeffEmb L ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L81), the $j$-series with coefficients transported from $\mathbb{Q}$, and to be nonzero. Further, $\varpi \in A$ generates $\mathfrak{m}_A$ (`hϖ`), and $\varpi_t \in A$ satisfies $\varpi_t^{\,q^2-1} = q\cdot u$ for some unit $u$ (`hϖt`).
--
--   Write $C =$ `chartAlgFin A ↥K j` for the $j$-finite chart algebra, the $A$-subalgebra of elements of $K$ integral over $A[j]$, with distinguished element `jChartFin A ↥K j` $= j$, and $X =$ [`AlgebraicCurve.TwoChartIntegralModel A ↥K j`](def/AlgebraicCurve_TwoChartIntegralModel.html#L236) for the scheme obtained by gluing $\operatorname{Spec} C$ and $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the $j^{-1}$-chart along the common middle chart, with structure morphism `toBase` to $\operatorname{Spec} A$ and with $\iota_{\mathrm{Fin}} : \operatorname{Spec} C \to X$. An ideal $y \subseteq C$ is given which is maximal (`hy`) and contains the image of $\varpi$ (`hϖy`), and which is supersingular in the following sense (`hss`): for every algebraically closed field $\Omega$ of characteristic $q$ and every ring homomorphism $\varphi : C \to \Omega$ with kernel $y$, the element $\varphi(j)$ lies in [`ModularCurve.ssJSet q Ω`](def/ModularCurve_SupersingularModuli.html#L7), the set of those $j$-invariants for which every elliptic Weierstrass curve over $\Omega$ with that invariant has no nonzero $\Omega$-point killed by $q$.
--
--   The hypothesis `hArig` is the Drinfeld-chart rigidity package at all supersingular points of the special fibre, summarised here. It requires: for every point $z$ of $X$ at which the germ $\varpi_z$ of $\varpi$ lies in the maximal ideal of the stalk $\mathcal{O}_{X,z}$, and every point $y'$ of $\operatorname{Spec} C$ with $\iota_{\mathrm{Fin}}(y') = z$ whose ideal satisfies the same supersingularity condition as $y$, there exist a complete discrete valuation ring $W$ which is a domain, a ring homomorphism $\sigma : A \to W$ with $\mathfrak{m}_W = (\sigma\varpi)$, power series $f, u, v \in W[[X_0,X_1]]$ with $u, v$ units and $f \equiv$ [`DrinfeldCurve.LocalChart.drinfeldForm q W`](def/DrinfeldCurve_LocalChart.html#L18) $= X_0X_1^q - X_0^qX_1$ modulo $(X_0,X_1)^{q+2}$, and a ring isomorphism $e$ from the $\mathfrak{m}$-adic completion of $\mathcal{O}_{X,z}$ onto $S = W[[X_0,X_1]]/(C(\sigma(\varpi_t^{q+1}))\,v - f\,u)$, such that, writing $\mathrm{toC}$ for the completion map, $\mathrm{mk}_S$ for the quotient map and $\mathrm{germ}_Y : C \to \mathcal{O}_{X,z}$ for the germ homomorphism through $\iota_{\mathrm{Fin}}$ at $y'$: (i) $e$ carries the germ of each $a \in A$ to the class of $C(\sigma a)$; (ii) for $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$, every $\tau \in \mathrm{Aut}_L(K)$ with [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.IsLevelAutAt L q ζ q (q ^ 2 * M') H₁ γ⁻¹ K τ`](def/ModularCurve_FullLevelLevelAutAt.html#L29) — that is, $\tau$ acts on quotients of integral $q$-expansions of modular forms of level `GammaH (q ^ 2 * M') H₁` by the substitution attached to the matrix $!![\gamma_{00}, \gamma_{01}/q; q\gamma_{10}, \gamma_{11}]$ for $\gamma^{-1}$, read through any embedding $\iota$ as above — preserves $C$; (iii) if moreover $\gamma_{11} \equiv 1 \pmod{\ell}$, the induced endomorphism of $C$ is congruent to the identity modulo $y'$; (iv) for $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ and $\tau$ as in (ii) which is congruent to the identity modulo $y'$, there are a ring automorphism $\theta$ of $S$, a scalar $c \in W$ and a matrix $M \in M_2(W)$ with: $\theta$ transporting $\tau$ through $e \circ \mathrm{toC} \circ \mathrm{germ}_Y$, $\theta$ fixing the constants, $\theta(X_j) \equiv \sum_i M_{ij}X_i$ modulo the square of the ideal generated by the classes of $X_0, X_1$, $c^{q+1} \equiv 1$ and $M_{ij} \equiv c\,\gamma_{ij}$ modulo $\mathfrak{m}_W$, $c \equiv 1$ whenever $\gamma_{11} \equiv 1 \pmod{\ell}$, and $c \not\equiv 1$ whenever $\gamma \in \Gamma(q)$ and $\tau \neq \mathrm{id}$; (v) branch separation: if $P_1, P_2$ are primes of $S$, neither containing both classes of $X_0$ and $X_1$, both containing the class of $C(\sigma\varpi)$, and $P_i$ contains an element with linear part $a_iX_0 + b_iX_1$ (error in $(X_0,X_1)^2$) with $q \nmid a_1b_2 - a_2b_1$, then the contractions of $P_1$ and $P_2$ to $\mathcal{O}_{X,z}$ along $e \circ \mathrm{toC}$ differ; (vi) a valuation criterion: for a prime $P$ of $S$ as in (v) containing the class of $C(\sigma\varpi)$ and an element with linear part $X_0$, an element $a \in C$ has $\mathrm{toC}(\mathrm{germ}_Y(a))$ in the contraction of $P$ along $e$ if and only if every Laurent coefficient of $a$ lies in the image of $\mathfrak{m}_A$; (vii) a Hasse-invariant clause: [`ModularCurve.jqNModC L q`](def/ModularCurve_JqCoeff.html#L18), the $j$-series with exponents scaled by $q$, lies in $K$ and in $C$, and there are $a_0 \in A$ with the difference lying in $y'$, an integer $e_0 \ge 1$ and $h \in (X_0,X_1)^{e_0}$ such that the degree-$e_0$ form $\sum_{i} \mathrm{coeff}_{(i,e_0-i)}(h)\,a^ib^{e_0-i}$ is a unit of $W$ for all $a, b \in W$ with at least one of $a,b$ a unit and $a^qb - ab^q \in \mathfrak{m}_W$, and such that $e(\mathrm{toC}(\mathrm{germ}_Y(\mathrm{jqNModC} - a_0)))$ is the class of $h$.
--
--   A particular point is then fixed: $z$, the germ $\varpi_z$ of $\varpi$ at $z$ lying in the maximal ideal of $\mathcal{O}_{X,z}$, a point $y'$ of $\operatorname{Spec} C$ with $\iota_{\mathrm{Fin}}(y') = z$, satisfying the supersingularity condition `hss'` and $y'.\mathrm{asIdeal} = y$ (`hy'y`). For this point an explicit chart presentation is given: a complete discrete valuation domain $W_1$, a homomorphism $\sigma_1 : A \to W_1$ with $\mathfrak{m}_{W_1} = (\sigma_1\varpi)$, series $f_1, u_1, v_1$ with $u_1, v_1$ units and $f_1$ congruent to the Drinfeld form modulo $(X_0,X_1)^{q+2}$, and an isomorphism $e_1$ from the adic completion of $\mathcal{O}_{X,z}$ onto $S = W_1[[X_0,X_1]]/(C(\sigma_1(\varpi_t^{q+1}))v_1 - f_1u_1)$; the hypothesis `hW₁` asserts, for this data, exactly the list of clauses (i)–(vii) above.
--
--   Finally, $J \subseteq C$ is an ideal required (`hJ`) to be the infimum of all ideals of the form $$\mathrm{comap}_{\tau|_C}\bigl(\mathrm{comap}_{e_1 \circ \mathrm{toC} \circ \mathrm{germ}_Y}\bigl(\mathrm{mk}_S(C(\sigma_1\varpi_t)),\ \mathrm{mk}_S(X_0),\ \mathrm{mk}_S(X_1)\bigr)\bigr),$$ taken over all $\gamma \in \Gamma(q) \cap \Gamma_0(M')$ and all $\tau \in \mathrm{Aut}_L(K)$ with `IsLevelAutAt L q ζ q (q ^ 2 * M') H₁ γ⁻¹ K τ` preserving $C$.
--
--   Under these hypotheses there exist an $A$-subalgebra $B$ of $K$, a valuation subring $W$ of $K$, and an inclusion $B \subseteq W$, such that all of the following hold.
--
--   First, $B$ is the $A$-subalgebra underlying the $C$-algebra generated by $\{x \in K : x\,\varpi_t \in J\}$, that is $B = C[J/\varpi_t]$, where membership is stated as the existence of $i \in J$ with $x\,\varpi_t = i$. Second, $C \le B$. Third, every $f \in K$ can be written as $g/h$ with $g, h \in B$ and $h \neq 0$. Fourth, $B$ is formally smooth over $A$. Fifth, $B$ is of finite presentation over $A$. Sixth, the special fibre $B/\varpi B$ has Krull dimension at most $1$.
--
--   Seventh, for $x \in L$ one has $x \in W$ (through $L \to K$) if and only if $x$ lies in the image of $A$; so $W$ contracts to $A$ on $L$. Eighth, the maximal ideal of $W$ is generated by the image of $\varpi$. Ninth, $W$ is a discrete valuation ring. Tenth, for $b \in C$, $b \in y$ if and only if $b$ lies in $W$ and in the maximal ideal of $W$; thus the centre of $W$ cuts out $y$ on $C$. Eleventh, for $f \in K$, $f \in W$ if and only if $f = g/h$ with $g, h \in B$ and $h$ a unit of $W$, i.e. $W$ is the localisation of $B$ at the centre of $W$.
--
--   This is the construction of the weighted blow-up chart $C[J/\varpi_t]$ of the $j$-finite chart algebra of the integral two-chart model along the orbit ideal $J$ attached to the supersingular point $y$, together with the exceptional discrete valuation it carries: the blown-up chart is formally smooth and of finite presentation over $A$ with one-dimensional special fibre, has $K$ as fraction field, and the exceptional valuation ring is the local ring of the chart at the centre lying over $y$. It is the variant of this construction for an arbitrary prime $q$ in which the auxiliary full level is replaced by a diamond condition at a prime $\ell \equiv 11 \pmod{12}$ dividing $M'$, and it feeds the assembly statement [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.AuxLevelOne.exists_supersingularAffineChart_ends_moduliHasse_commonChart_orbitPoles_inertia_chartAlgFin_of_stalk_drinfeldChart_moduliHasse_igusaSep_deckSep_linkedScalars_linkedInertia_of_dvd`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.AuxLevelOne.exists_supersingularAffineChart_ends_moduliHasse_commonChart_orbitPoles_inertia_chartAlgFin_of_stalk_drinfeldChart_moduliHasse_igusaSep_deckSep_linkedScalars_linkedInertia_of_dvd).
